{"type":"text","timestamp":1777647958884,"sessionID":"ses_21bede0e1ffe7OwCW9XRNWd6M4","part":{"id":"prt_de4131bf9001OBuZ0589PIB7qk","messageID":"msg_de4131641001AWeM9QsTKuxSxD","sessionID":"ses_21bede0e1ffe7OwCW9XRNWd6M4","type":"text","text":"Now I need to synthesize the factual findings from the subagent and formulate a concise final answer to the user's multi-hop question.\n</think>\n\nBased on the documents, here is the answer:\n\n**The country is Poland**, which satisfies both conditions:\n1. The Warsaw Pact's Combined Command of Pact Armed Forces had its headquarters in Warsaw, Poland\n2. Poland historically had the \"nobilities commonwealth\" (Poland's szlachta/nobility, described in Paragraph 5 as \"Poland was called the nobility's Commonwealth\")\n\n**Poland agreed to join NATO on March 12, 1999**, as part of the fourth NATO enlargement that also included Hungary and the Czech Republic. This was under the context of unified Germany's NATO membership:\n\n- East Germany had already been included in NATO in 1990 with German reunification (Paragraph 25)\n- Poland, Czech Republic, and Hungary were invited in 1997 and joined in the 1999 enlargement (Paragraph 8)\n\nThe unified Germany itself became a NATO member in 1955 (Paragraph 8), and Poland later joined NATO in 1999 as a former Warsaw Pact country.\n\n**Answer: 1999** (specifically March 12, 1999)","time":{"start":1777647958880,"end":1777647958880}}}
